**Why:** He wants a clean separation; wafa attribution leaked into main repos because the Mac's global git config was set to wafa's identity (fixed 2026-07-03 to Taha-Mahmoodi / 85902429+Taha-Mahmoodi@users.noreply.github.com). With a third account added 2026-07-05, the same leak risk applies in both directions — don't let sadqi's account become active for Taha's own work, or vice versa.

**Exception — third-eye-world-mono v1 (2026-07-20):** Taha explicitly directed that **PRs on `Taha-Mahmoodi/third-eye-world-mono` be opened from Said's account** (`sadeqisaidmohaddes-star`, a write-access collaborator there). So the active gh account for `gh pr create`/`merge` on that repo is sadqi, while **commits stay authored as Taha-Mahmoodi**. This is deliberate, not a leak — it supersedes the older "Said credit only on the paper repo" rule for this repo. Still switch back to Taha-Mahmoodi before touching anything else. See [[third-eye-world-mono]].

**How to apply:** If commits ever show the wrong identity, check `git config user.email` (global and per-repo) first. Closed atlas-erp PRs #90–#122 permanently show wafa in their commit snapshots — known, accepted limitation. `gh` CLI has all three accounts logged in; default active account should be Taha-Mahmoodi — after doing anything as sadqi or wafa, switch back with `gh auth switch --hostname github.com --user Taha-Mahmoodi` and verify with `gh auth status`.
